### Describe the bug

When defining a relation like so
```ts
const FooSchema = defineEntity({
    name: "foo",
    properties: {
        id: p.integer().primary(),
        my_bar: () => p.oneToOne(BarSchema).lazy().fieldName("bar_id") // here 
    }
})
```
TypeScript 7 language server starts having extreme latency. If lazy() is called last, then the latency is reduced significantly.

### Reproduction

```ts
import { p, defineEntity, defineConfig, MikroORM } from "@mikro-orm/sqlite"

const FooEntity = defineEntity({
    name: "foo",
    properties: {
        id: p.integer().primary(),
        my_bar: () => p.oneToOne(BarEntity).lazy().fieldName("bar_id")
        // swap the call order of lazyRef and fieldName
    }
})

const BarEntity = defineEntity({
    name: "bar",
    properties: {
        id: p.integer().primary()
    }
})

const orm = await MikroORM.init(defineConfig({
    dbName: ":memory:",
    entities: [FooEntity, BarEntity]
}))

const em = orm.em.fork()

const match = await em.findOne(FooEntity, { id: 3}, { populate: ["my_bar.*"] })
```

Swapping around the call shows the difference in latency,

