Hi @B4nan,
I found a bug a weird bug while working on my project and Fable traced it into MikroORM internals. Below are its findings - the attached [PR](https://github.com/mikro-orm/mikro-orm/pull/8177) makes the bug go away, however I'm not that familiar with the MikroORM codebase to saying for sure that's the right way to do it; if it's not - do tell :)

## Describe the bug

With standard (TC39) decorators, a `@Check` declared on an entity that extends a base class is silently missing from `MetadataStorage` and from all generated DDL whenever **any ancestor class has at least one `@Property`-decorated field**. No error or warning is emitted — the entity's metadata simply ends up with `checks: []`, and `getCreateSchemaSQL()` / migrations contain no CHECK constraint. All three declaration styles are affected: class-level `@Check`, property-level `@Check`, and the `check` option of `@Property`.

A base class whose only decorated member is `@PrimaryKey` does **not** trigger the bug (only `@Property` seeds the `checks` array, see below).

### Root cause

`context.metadata` of a subclass is created with the parent class's metadata object as its **prototype**. The decorators in `@mikro-orm/decorators/es` initialize their collections with an unguarded `??=`, and `@Entity()` transfers only own properties, so:

1. [Property.ts#L29](https://github.com/mikro-orm/mikro-orm/blob/ee849df64b434f460a10d65eb1ac058e8bbcd84c/packages/decorators/src/es/Property.ts#L29) https://github.com/mikro-orm/mikro-orm/blob/ee849df64b434f460a10d65eb1ac058e8bbcd84c/packages/decorators/src/es/Property.ts#L29 — `meta.checks ??= [];` runs unconditionally, so every class with ≥ 1 `@Property` gets an **own** `checks: []` on its decorator metadata.
2. [Check.ts#L12](https://github.com/mikro-orm/mikro-orm/blob/ee849df64b434f460a10d65eb1ac058e8bbcd84c/packages/decorators/src/es/Check.ts#L12) https://github.com/mikro-orm/mikro-orm/blob/ee849df64b434f460a10d65eb1ac058e8bbcd84c/packages/decorators/src/es/Check.ts#L12 — on the subclass, the `meta.checks ??= []` *read* resolves the ancestor's (non-nullish) array through the prototype chain, so no own array is ever created; the subsequent `meta.checks.push(options)` ([`[Check.ts#L18](https://github.com/mikro-orm/mikro-orm/blob/ee849df64b434f460a10d65eb1ac058e8bbcd84c/packages/decorators/src/es/Check.ts#L18)`](https://github.com/mikro-orm/mikro-orm/blob/ee849df64b434f460a10d65eb1ac058e8bbcd84c/packages/decorators/src/es/Check.ts#L18)) **mutates the base class's metadata**.
3. [Entity.ts#L10](https://github.com/mikro-orm/mikro-orm/blob/ee849df64b434f460a10d65eb1ac058e8bbcd84c/packages/decorators/src/es/Entity.ts#L10) https://github.com/mikro-orm/mikro-orm/blob/ee849df64b434f460a10d65eb1ac058e8bbcd84c/packages/decorators/src/es/Entity.ts#L10 — `{ ...context.metadata }` copies own enumerable properties only, so the prototype-resident `checks` never reaches `MetadataStorage` for the subclass.

Side effect of step 2: if the base class is itself an `@Entity`, the subclass's check **leaks into the base entity's metadata** — `Utils.mergeConfig` assigns arrays by reference, so the base's `MetadataStorage` entry shares the very array the subclass later pushes into, and the constraint can be emitted on the wrong table.

### Same latent bug in every other TC39 metadata collection

The identical unguarded pattern exists for the remaining collections. Each is dormant until an ancestor happens to own the collection — then every subclass-level declaration silently vanishes (and leaks to the base) the same way:

- [Indexed.ts#L15-L16](https://github.com/mikro-orm/mikro-orm/blob/ee849df64b434f460a10d65eb1ac058e8bbcd84c/packages/decorators/src/es/Indexed.ts#L15-L16) https://github.com/mikro-orm/mikro-orm/blob/ee849df64b434f460a10d65eb1ac058e8bbcd84c/packages/decorators/src/es/Indexed.ts#L15-L16 — `indexes` / `uniques`: triggered as soon as any ancestor field has `@Index`/`@Unique`. Verified on master: a single `@Index` on a base-class field makes every child-level `@Index`/`@Unique` disappear from the generated schema.
- [Trigger.ts#L9-L10](https://github.com/mikro-orm/mikro-orm/blob/ee849df64b434f460a10d65eb1ac058e8bbcd84c/packages/decorators/src/es/Trigger.ts#L9-L10) https://github.com/mikro-orm/mikro-orm/blob/ee849df64b434f460a10d65eb1ac058e8bbcd84c/packages/decorators/src/es/Trigger.ts#L9-L10 — `triggers`: triggered when an ancestor class has `@Trigger`.
- [hooks.ts#L6-L8](https://github.com/mikro-orm/mikro-orm/blob/ee849df64b434f460a10d65eb1ac058e8bbcd84c/packages/decorators/src/es/hooks.ts#L6-L8) https://github.com/mikro-orm/mikro-orm/blob/ee849df64b434f460a10d65eb1ac058e8bbcd84c/packages/decorators/src/es/hooks.ts#L6-L8 — `hooks`: a two-level variant (`meta.hooks ??= {}` plus `meta.hooks[type] ??= []`). Verified on master: with a `@BeforeCreate` on a base class, a subclass entity ends up with **no hooks at all** — neither the base's nor its own fire.

`properties` is the one collection that already has the correct guard: `prepareMetadataContext` (`[utils.ts#L119-L121](https://github.com/mikro-orm/mikro-orm/blob/ee849df64b434f460a10d65eb1ac058e8bbcd84c/packages/decorators/src/utils.ts#L119-L121)` (https://github.com/mikro-orm/mikro-orm/blob/ee849df64b434f460a10d65eb1ac058e8bbcd84c/packages/decorators/src/utils.ts#L119-L121)) creates an own copy behind `Object.hasOwn`, added in 363b4af73 for #7093 — its doc comment even names the hazard. The other collections never got the same treatment. #7982 (class-level `@Check` crash under TC39 decorators) is adjacent but did not cover this: its regression test has no inheritance.

Legacy decorators (`@mikro-orm/decorators/legacy`) are **not** affected — they write to per-class `MetadataStorage` entries directly.

### Expected behavior

Checks/indexes/uniques/triggers/hooks declared on a subclass reach `MetadataStorage` and the generated DDL regardless of what its base classes declare — or, at minimum, a loud error instead of a silent drop.

### Suggested fix

Mirror the existing `properties` handling: initialize each collection behind `Object.hasOwn`, creating an own array that copies the inherited items. Copying is safe for base entities — `MetadataDiscovery` merges base-entity collections with identity-based `Utils.unique` ([MetadataDiscovery.ts#L1396-L1401](https://github.com/mikro-orm/mikro-orm/blob/ee849df64b434f460a10d65eb1ac058e8bbcd84c/packages/core/src/metadata/MetadataDiscovery.ts#L1396-L1401) https://github.com/mikro-orm/mikro-orm/blob/ee849df64b434f460a10d65eb1ac058e8bbcd84c/packages/core/src/metadata/MetadataDiscovery.ts#L1396-L1401), so shared references dedupe — and it is what preserves declarations from non-entity base classes for the child. I have a branch with failing tests plus this fix ready and will open a PR right after filing this issue.


The bug is driver-independent (it lives in `@mikro-orm/decorators`); the same file against `@mikro-orm/sqlite` with `dbName: ':memory:'` behaves identically. A failing test against master demonstrating all affected collections (checks, indexes, uniques, triggers, hooks) can be found inside the [PR](https://github.com/mikro-orm/mikro-orm/pull/8177).

