  @PrimaryKey()
  id!: number;

  @ManyToOne(() => Author, { mapToPk: true })
  author!: number;
}

const em = orm.em.fork();
em.create(Book, { id: 1, author: 0 });
await em.flush(); // RangeError: Maximum call stack size exceeded
```
Deterministic on current master with better-sqlite; any driver should reproduce since the loop is driver-independent.

**Root cause**
`ChangeSetComputer.processProperty` guards with `if (!target)` — a raw FK of `0` is falsy, so it's treated as "no target" and the unwrap branch re-enters itself forever. `Utils.unwrapProperty` only yields non-null values and `processToOne` early-returns for `mapToPk`, so relaxing the guard to `target == null` is behavior-safe for `0`/`''`/`false`.

Related: #8000 covers the read side of the same falsy-FK class (1:m collections not populated when the parent PK is `0`). This one is the write side and is a hard crash.

I have a fix with a regression test ready and will open a PR right after this issue.

