## Describe the bug

`AbstractSqlDriver.mapJoinedProp` throws `TypeError: pk.every is not a function` during a joined `find()` / `getResultList()` whenever a relation property has `fieldNames.length > 1` (so it takes the composite-key branch) but `Utils.mapFlatCompositePrimaryKey` resolves the target meta down to a **single** primary prop and therefore returns a **scalar** instead of an array.

```
TypeError: pk.every is not a function
    at PostgreSqlDriver.mapJoinedProp (@mikro-orm/sql/AbstractSqlDriver.js)
```

## Root cause

The composite-key branch in `mapJoinedProp` assumes the return value is always an array and casts it as such before calling `.every`:

`packages/sql/src/AbstractSqlDriver.ts` (master):

```ts
} else if (prop.fieldNames.length > 1) {
  // composite keys
  const fk = prop.fieldNames.map(name => root[`${relationAlias}__${name}` as EntityKey<T>]) as Primary<T>[];
  const pk = Utils.mapFlatCompositePrimaryKey(fk, prop) as unknown[];        // <-- cast hides the scalar case
  relationPojo[prop.name] = pk.every(val => val != null) ? (pk as EntityDataValue<T>) : null;
}
```

But `Utils.mapFlatCompositePrimaryKey` is explicitly typed to return either shape, and unwraps to a scalar when `parts.length < 2`:

`packages/core/src/utils/Utils.ts` (master):

```ts
static mapFlatCompositePrimaryKey(
  fk: Primary<any>[],
  prop: EntityProperty,
  fieldNames = prop.fieldNames,
  idx = 0,
): Primary<any> | Primary<any>[] {
  if (!prop.targetMeta) {
    return fk[idx++];                 // scalar
  }
  const parts: Primary<any>[] = [];
  for (const pk of prop.targetMeta.getPrimaryProps()) {
    parts.push(this.mapFlatCompositePrimaryKey(fk, pk, fieldNames, idx));
    idx += pk.fieldNames.length;
  }
  if (parts.length < 2) {
    return parts[0];                  // unwraps to a scalar
  }
  return parts;
}
```

## Expected behavior

`mapJoinedProp` should handle both return shapes of `mapFlatCompositePrimaryKey` — a scalar PK should be assigned directly (or `null` when it is nullish), without calling array methods on it.

We currently ship this as a `patch-package` patch against `@mikro-orm/sql`.

