### Describe the bug

Hello,

I don't know if it's an expected behavior, it kinda make some sense in a way. But it caused some bug in production in one of our app. 

When an @Embeddable class is instantiated with new EmbeddableClass() and none of its         
  properties have been assigned a value (they are undefined), the UOW changeset payload differs
   depending on the object flag of the parent @Embedded decorator:

  - object: true → the payload contains billing: {} — an empty object is always written by the 
  snapshot generator, even when every child property is undefined
  - object: false → the payload contains nothing for the embedded field — no flattened column  
  key is written, so the field is simply absent                                                

  @Embeddable()                                                                                
