### Describe the bug

With `resultCache.global` enabled, every `em.find()` triggers **two** `set()` calls on the cache adapter — one keyed `[entityName, 'em.find', ...]`, one keyed `['qb.execute', sql, params, method]`. v6.4.x triggered one.

### Cause

PR #6923 (streaming) added `options.em as any` to the internal `createQueryBuilder(...)` call in `AbstractSqlDriver.find()`. That activated previously-dormant `this.em?.tryCache(...)` / `this.em?.storeCache(...)` calls in `QueryBuilder.execute()` — in v6.4.x `this.em` was `undefined` there, so the QB-level cache calls silently no-op'd. Verified locally: reverting only that one argument restores single-`set()` behavior.

> Side note: the QB-level cache key omits `entityName`, so per-entity invalidation from a custom adapter isn't possible on those entries even if the duplicate write is intentional.

### Versions
- last working: v6.4.13
- broken: v7.0.0+


